# Allowlist of the secret scan (scripts/secret_scan.py, CONTRIBUTING.md section 6).
#
# The scan reports every value in a provider's exact token format, even an obviously fake one, because GitHub push
# protection blocks such values. Old commits cannot be changed without rewriting the history, so this file names the
# documented test mocks that are already in them. Rules:
#
# - Only documented test mocks. Never a real credential, however old or revoked: rotate it and rewrite the history
#   instead (CONTRIBUTING.md section 12). No password, IP address, host name or personal data either.
# - Entries apply to --history only (CI, make secret-scan). Every other mode (files, tracked files, --staged,
#   --push) still reports the value, so the git hooks stop a new commit that contains it: GitHub may block it.
# - An entry drops the exact-format finding of its own value and nothing else. A longer value of another format
#   around it is still reported. The other rules (provider key rules, local patterns, forbidden file names) never
#   drop a finding because of this file, so a real-looking key is reported even if its digest is listed here, and
#   they also read the line without the listed value, so a value next to a mock cannot pass as a placeholder.
# - An entry names exactly one value by the sha256 hex digest of that exact value, never the value itself (that
#   would be an exact-format literal that GitHub blocks). Compute the digest without the value in your shell history:
#     python3 -c "import getpass, hashlib; print(hashlib.sha256(getpass.getpass('value: ').encode()).hexdigest())"
# - Format of an entry, one per line: 64 lower-case hex digits, two spaces, then the note
#     <first 4 characters>...<last 4 characters> (<length> chars): <why it is a mock and where it is>
#   A malformed line stops the scan in every mode (exit 2), so a typo cannot silently allow more. Lines end at a
#   line feed (CRLF too); a control, format or line separator character other than a tab (a lone carriage return,
#   a byte order mark, a zero-width space) makes a line malformed, so a comment cannot hide an entry.
#   Lines starting with "#" are comments.

